From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Apex <apex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] elan: Retry transient pre-scan status on 04f3:0c6e

The 04f3:0c6e answers pre_scan_cmd with 0x00 (not ready) or 0xaf
(sensor busy or finger removed), as the 0x0c58 does. Only the 0x0c58
retries these answers. On the 0x0c6e they fail the session with
FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO, which fprintd reports as enroll-disconnected,
most often on the duplicate-check identify that precedes an enrollment.

Give the 0x0c6e its own quirk bit and turn the 0x0c58-only check in
CAPTURE_READ_DATA into the mask ELAN_RETRY_TRANSIENT_STATUS. The new
device needs its own bit because ELAN_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS() and other
checks compare dev_type for equality. Also log the pre-scan status byte
at debug level, so that a log shows which answer a sensor gives.

No other device changes behaviour. The elan umockdev tests replay an
0x0c26 and only gain the new debug line.

The retry is unbounded, as it is for the 0x0c58 today; the next patch
bounds it.

Equivalent to ssubbotin/libfprint@5a89584b (libfprint#814), and a
subset of MR !655.

Refs: libfprint#879 #814 #808 #732 #402 #763
---
 libfprint/drivers/elan.c |    7 +++++--
 libfprint/drivers/elan.h |   10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
index f9cc52f75ebd..21452c980592 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -552,16 +552,19 @@ capture_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
     case CAPTURE_READ_DATA:
       /* 0x55 - finger present
        * 0xff - device not calibrated (probably) */
+      if (self->last_read)
+        fp_dbg ("pre-scan status: 0x%02x", self->last_read[0]);
+
       if (self->last_read && self->last_read[0] == 0x55)
         {
           fpi_image_device_report_finger_status (idev, TRUE);
           elan_run_cmd (ssm, dev, &get_image_cmd, ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT);
         }
-      else if (self->dev_type == ELAN_0C58 && self->last_read &&
+      else if ((self->dev_type & ELAN_RETRY_TRANSIENT_STATUS) && self->last_read &&
                (self->last_read[0] == 0x00 || self->last_read[0] == 0xaf))
         {
           /* 0x00 - not ready
-           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58) */
+           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58 and 0x0c6e) */
           fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER, 10);
         }
       else
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
index 6bbaae04888f..446ccc58f739 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
@@ -32,10 +32,18 @@
 #define ELAN_0C03 (1 << 1)
 #define ELAN_0C42 (1 << 2)
 #define ELAN_0C58 (1 << 3)
+#define ELAN_0C6E (1 << 4)
 
 /* devices which don't require frame rotation before assembling */
 #define ELAN_NOT_ROTATED ELAN_0C03
 
+/* devices that answer pre_scan_cmd with transient status bytes (0x00 - not
+ * ready, 0xaf - sensor busy or finger already removed) instead of 0x55 or a
+ * read timeout. These must be retried rather than treated as a protocol
+ * error. Seen on 0x0c58 (libfprint#763) and 0x0c6e (libfprint#814, #808,
+ * #879). */
+#define ELAN_RETRY_TRANSIENT_STATUS (ELAN_0C58 | ELAN_0C6E)
+
 /* min FW version that supports calibration */
 #define ELAN_MIN_CALIBRATION_FW 0x0138
 
@@ -222,7 +230,7 @@ static const FpIdEntry elan_id_table[] = {
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4d, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4f, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c63, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
-  {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c6e, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
+  {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c6e, .driver_data = ELAN_0C6E},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c58, .driver_data = ELAN_0C58},
   {.vid = 0,  .pid = 0,  .driver_data = 0},
 };
